  ('372755f4-fbca-5232-b0d6-04ba69821d05', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The prefix pro- means "forward," and the Latin root pel means "push" or "drive." What does it mean that the riders felt "propelled along the empty road"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They felt held back by a strong force in front","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They felt pulled off the road toward the side","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"They felt driven forward by a force behind them","is_correct":true},{"text":"They felt too tired to keep moving any longer","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They felt driven forward by a force behind them$q$, $q$Pro- plus pel means "drive forward," and the tailwind made them feel "as if someone were pushing them." Being held back by a force in front would describe a headwind, the opposite of what the passage says.$q$, 'draft', '0b0f8aee-e3a6-5cc5-afe9-bac2868278d6')
