   $q$The Latin root rect means "straight" or "right," as in a right angle. What is a "rectangular glass block"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A block that has been broken into sections","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-roots"},{"text":"A block with smooth, rounded, curving sides","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A block with straight sides and square corners","is_correct":true},{"text":"A block made from very thick, colored glass","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A block with straight sides and square corners$q$, $q$Rect means "straight" or "right," so a rectangular block has straight edges that meet at right angles, and the passage mentions its "flat side." Rounded, curving sides are the opposite of straight.$q$, 'draft', '70e536f5-ef5f-5631-8450-c7ac7df9f16a')
