   $q$The prefix re- can mean "again," and son means "sound." What does it mean that the chord seemed to "resonate through the whole room"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The sound kept echoing and ringing through the room","is_correct":true},{"text":"The sound was too loud for the players to stand","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The sound faded out the moment the bows stopped","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The sound was played a second time by the strings","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The sound kept echoing and ringing through the room$q$, $q$Re- plus son means "sound again," so the chord kept sounding, "ringing off the wooden walls and lingering in the air after the bows had stopped." Fading at once is the opposite of lingering.$q$, 'draft', '010113db-f97d-53bd-893b-4116d3ab8a16')
