   $q$The prefix trans- means "across," and the Latin root fer means "carry." What are riders doing when they are "transferring to the downtown line"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Waiting half an hour for the next bus to come","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Carrying heavy bags across the transit center","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Moving from one bus to another to keep traveling","is_correct":true},{"text":"Paying an extra fare to ride the downtown line","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Moving from one bus to another to keep traveling$q$, $q$Trans- plus fer means "carry across," so riders carry themselves across from one bus to another, walking "a few steps to the next bus." Waiting half an hour is what the plan is designed to avoid.$q$, 'draft', '8322960e-ac2d-515a-aa45-ae32e3bdf95f')
