   $q$The Latin root mar means "sea." What is a "maritime museum"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A museum about old buildings and warehouses","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A museum about the history of measuring time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-words"},{"text":"A museum about rivers that run through towns","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad-context"},{"text":"A museum about ships, sailing and the sea","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A museum about ships, sailing and the sea$q$, $q$Mar means "sea," and the museum holds "old fishing boats, ship models and brass instruments." The "time" in maritime is not the word time, so a museum about clocks ignores the root.$q$, 'draft', 'd9f9c526-c701-5695-880f-42fe4452c2d2')
